.\" Manpage for git-subtree-report-1
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0
.Dd July 09, 2025
.Dt GIT-SUBTREE-REPORT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm git-subtree-report-1
.Nd Analyze Git repositories/subtrees for safe file concatenation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl C Ar dir | Fl -working-dir=dir
.Op Fl e Ar pattern | Fl -exclude=pattern
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Op Fl i Ar pattern | Fl -include=pattern
.Op Fl o | Fl -output-concat
.Op Fl r Ar ref | Fl -ref=ref
.Op Fl s Ar size | Fl -max-size=size
.Op Fl t Ar path | Fl -subtree=path
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility performs deep analysis of Git repository subtrees to determine file safety for concatenation outputs. It operates directly on the Git object database without requiring a checkout. Key features include:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Full tree visualization with a two-stage filtering system.
.It
Multi-level safety checks (binary detection, encoding validation).
.It
Integration with Git LFS and submodules.
.It
Historical analysis at any commit reference.
.El
.Pp
Filters are applied in a sequence: first, the
.Fl i
(include) pattern creates an allow-list. Then, the
.Fl e
(exclude) pattern removes items from that list.
.Sh OPTIONS
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "--output-concat"
.It Fl C Ar dir , Fl -working-dir=dir
Change working directory before analysis. This is essential for operating on bare repositories.
.It Fl e Ar pattern , Fl -exclude=pattern
Exclude paths from the included set that match a given Extended Regular Expression (ERE). This block-list is applied *after* the include filter.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display the help message with all options and exit.
.It Fl i Ar pattern , Fl -include=pattern
Only include files matching a given ERE. This allow-list is applied first, before any exclusion patterns. If not provided, all files in the subtree are included by default.
.It Fl o , Fl -output-concat
Enable concatenation output mode. Instead of the summary report, this will print the content of all safe, concatenatable files to standard output, separated by headers.
.It Fl r Ar ref , Fl -ref=ref
Analyze the repository state at a specified Git reference (e.g., a branch name, tag, or commit SHA). Defaults to
.Ql HEAD .
.It Fl s Ar size , Fl -max-size=size
Set the maximum file size for detailed content analysis. Files larger than this will be skipped during safety checks. The size can be specified in human-readable format (e.g., 5M, 100K, 1G). Defaults to 1M.
.It Fl t Ar path , Fl -subtree=path
Specify a subdirectory path to analyze, relative to the repository root. If not provided, the script analyzes from the current directory's location within the repository.
.It Fl -version
Display the version number of the script and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LC_ALL
Overrides locale settings. The script requires a UTF-8 compatible locale, such as
.Ql C.UTF-8 ,
to be available for correct text processing.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If this variable is set to any value, colored output in the terminal is disabled.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/git-subtree-report-1
Typical installation path for the executable.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Analyze only C/C++ source files in the
.Ql src/
directory, while excluding any from test subdirectories:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report-1 -t src/ -i '\\.(c|h)$' -e '/test/'
.Pp
Generate a concatenated output for all text files in the
.Ql docs/
directory for a quick audit:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report-1 -t docs/ -o | less -R
.Pp
Analyze project state from 3 months ago:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report-1 -r $(git rev-list -n1 --until="3 months ago" main)
.Pp
Perform a security audit using long options for clarity:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report-1 --working-dir /srv/app --subtree api/ --exclude '\\.secret(s)?$' --output-concat > api_audit.txt
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr perl 1 ,
.Xr numfmt 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Cameron Garnham Aq Mt me@da2ce7.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Special considerations for repository types:
.Bl -bullet
.It
For bare repositories, you must either invoke the script from the repository's root directory or use the
.Fl C
option to specify the full path to the repository (e.g.,
.Pa /path/to/bare/repo.git ) .
.It
When combining
.Fl C
and
.Fl t ,
the path for
.Fl C
must always point to the repository root, not a subdirectory within it.
.It
All path operations are contained within the repository and prevent upward traversal (e.g., using
.Ql ../ ) .
.El
